The \([A^4]E\) problem is deeper than omission: its printed formula is algebraically wrong. Re-expansion yields coefficients \(-F\eta-4ZF\eta'\), not \(-3F\eta-8ZF\eta'\). The corrected equation actually collapses to the stronger algebraic relation
\[
2c_2(D_1-D_2')=3c_1\eta(E_1-E_2'),
\]
so the residual can be repaired cleanly—but it is seven free polynomials/seven lower identities (or eight/eight), not eight/seven.
