+Here is exactly where coprimality enters. If
+`gcd(∂p,∂r)=1`, choose `a,b in C[Z]` with `a∂r+b∂p=1`. For any `W`,
+`(X,Y)=(aW,-bW)` solves `X∂r-∂pY=W`. Conversely coprimality in the PID
